exp-15 — raising a replication factor under load, throttled and not
date: 2026-09-25-033634
topic: 3 partitions starting at RF 2, preloaded with 60 MiB; producers write one 1 KiB record every 10 ms

note: apply elects the preferred leader on the topics it touches
go run github.com/segmentio/topicctl/cmd/topicctl@v1.23.1 apply --cluster-config deploy/topicctl/cluster.yaml --skip-confirm experiments/kafka_internals/exp-15-partition-reassignment/topics/*.yaml
{{exp15.reassign kafka-lab local lab exp-15: a topic that starts at replication factor 2 so that the experiment can raise it
to 3 while producers are writing to it. min.insync.replicas is 1 here, not the catalog's
2: with two replicas a quorum of two leaves no room for one of them to be busy catching
up, and the run would measure a refused write instead of the cost of the move.

The catalog cannot host this. A reassignment rewrites replica placement, and topicctl
declines to change a replication factor at all — this is the experiment that shows why
that is a migration rather than a line in a YAML.
 map[] []} {3 2 60 map[min.insync.replicas:1 unclean.leader.election.enable:false] {any  [] []} <nil>}}
